+# Align Selection Quick Start
+
+Build: Witch Tools Dev_v2.7.0  
+Target: Blender 4.5.0
+
+## Match coordinates
+
+1. Select the source vertex, edge, face, or set.
+2. Choose Median or Active Element and click Capture Source.
+3. Select the geometry to align.
+4. Enable X, Y, and/or Z, choose Match Coordinates, and click Apply.
+
+## Preserve shape
+
+1. Capture the source.
+2. Select the wall or anchor geometry that must reach the source and click Capture Target Anchor(s). Multiple cavity anchors may be captured together.
+3. Select every vertex that must move with the anchor.
+4. Choose Translate / Preserve Shape. Use Per Connected Island for multiple separate cavities.
+5. Enable the required axes and click Apply.
+
+The operation evaluates coordinates in world space and converts results back into each edited object. Objects with non-basis shape keys are rejected before movement.
